WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.310
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:29.360
Today, as usual, it looks like Team Rocket
are up to something.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.390
What a nuisance...
We’re having an important meeting!

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.510
But can we really just
let it keep ringing?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.080
Agh...

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:38.970
Here goes...

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.570
<i>Sakaki!</i>

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.350
Calls are to be answered promptly.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.070
Oh, here I am wondering who could be calling,
and it’s his efficient secretary, Lady Matori.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.820
Where’s Sakaki?!

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.490
Did you want something?!

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:59.220
Are you aware that
we’re very busy right now?!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.380
Sakaki is currently in an important meeting
and can’t come to the phone.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.150
Then, goodbye.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.340
They might have needed us
for something important!

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.430
Hey!

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.590
I have orders for you from Sakaki.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.140
In recognition of your constant devotion
towards carrying out your missions,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.930
you will be granted a special break.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.600
This order is absolute.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.880
<i>Break?!</i>

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:34.690
PocketMonsters

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.110
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.690
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.410
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.280
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.620
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.290
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:54.790
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:00.050
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:04.640
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.560
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.310
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:21.320
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.530
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.870
Let's have a fight!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.580
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.410
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:35.750
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:42.420
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:47.760
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.260
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.390
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.190
I choose you!

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:05.200
Take a Break! Team Rocket!

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.080
Huh, that’s a pretty place.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.420
Director Sakuragi,
did something happen there?

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.840
This is the Resort Area
in the Sinnoh Region.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.200
Supposedly this lake is home to
a Pokémon known as “The Lord”.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.370
The Lord?!

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.720
What kind of Pokémon is it?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.660
We don’t really know.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:29.430
Sightings mention seeing
a massive shadow in the lake,

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.380
or that it jumped incredibly high.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.600
Apparently, lots of trainers
are gathering there to try and catch it!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.190
C’mon, Go!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.610
I wanna see this Lord Pokémon!

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.030
Yeah!
I’m gonna catch it for sure!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.750
Resort Area, the Sinnoh Region

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.120
The blue seas!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.500
The blue skies!

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.710
The green grass!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.590
<i>This is the best!</i>

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.090
What better place for a holiday
than a resort?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.470
This is true relaxation, meow!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.300
Sometimes you need time
to forget work and relax.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.750
Right! Let’s forget all about
the brat boy and Pikachu...

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.090
And relax, meow!

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.230
So this is the Resort Area?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.640
I wanna go for a swim!

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.150
We don’t have time
to go swimming!

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.100
What’s the brat boy...

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.040
...doing here?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.320
Umm, excuse me?

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.990
Yes?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.670
Where can we find this lake?

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.890
Oh, that lake is over there, me lads.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.410
Thank you!

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.950
Right this way, they said!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.770
Pikachu!
We’ll leave you behind!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.730
What are they doing here?!

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.250
They’re probably here
looking for Pokémon...

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.150
This is our chance
to catch Pikachu, meow!

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.540
No! We’re on break right now,
by order of Sakaki!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.430
Oh, right...
It’d be against orders...

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.110
Right, meow...

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.780
But, but... Pikachu’s right in front
of our eyes, meow...

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.660
We saw nothing.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.420
Let’s forget the brat boy and Pikachu,
and enjoy our break!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.030
Yeah!

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.480
Hmm... Which one is best...?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.370
Ack!
Hmm... Which one is best...?

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:24.430
Oh, you guys! Thanks for earlier!

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.390
Oh, it was nothi—

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:27.910
So what are you doing, me lads?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.640
We’re about to go fishing...

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.140
But we need to get
sturdy fishing rods.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.390
But we don’t know
what to choose...

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.170
Is that so!

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.870
Well, this rod here is
really good for beginners!

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:44.070
It’s sturdy and flexible!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.610
If you’re looking
to hook big fish...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:45.910
What is he doing?

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.290
Oh! This lure!
What is he doing?

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.280
Beats me...

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.770
Look out!

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:53.040
Watch where you’re going,
why don’t ya?!

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.160
Sorry!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:01.300
Oh, uh, you should
be careful, too...

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.560
Pikachu!

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.230
Here.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.170
Thank you.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.160
You thank her, too,
Pikachu!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.980
Y-You’re very welcome!

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.930
We found some great stuff!

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.140
I can get a bit obsessive
about fishing, me lads...

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.150
Thank you!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.520
Okay! Time to fish!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.280
I’m glad those kind people were here!

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.530
That was the perfect chance, meow...

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:29.250
I had Pikachu in the palm of my hand...!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.530
If we weren’t on holiday...!

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.420
Our mission is to
take a break, meow!

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.720
Good morning.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:44.720
How are preparations?

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.080
Complete.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:57.050
Sakaki’s ambition is to rule over everything,
and bring order to the world.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:01.570
To carry out this goal,
we will need exceptional Pokémon.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:06.400
Many of the tourists here
have rare or strong Pokémon.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.540
If we capture them all at once,
they’ll be a great asset to Team Rocket.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.250
I won’t stand for failure!

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.490
Exercise utmost caution!

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.630
Ma’am!

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.810
Sakaki said I could bring
as many agents as I want,

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:25.080
but my handpicked
elite unit is all I need.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.710
I don’t need any deadweight.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.480
What’s wrong, Musashi?

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.410
I just had this awful feeling...

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.760
Must’ve imagined it.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:34.830
But forget that...

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.910
Everyone here is trying to
fish up the Lord...

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.060
We’re not gonna lose!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.800
Looks like they’re fishing for
the Lord of this lake, meow...

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.610
I wanna fish it out!

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.440
Does it even really exist?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.860
I’ve got it!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.410
Already?!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.820
C’mon!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.200
A Tosakinto!

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:59.200
Tosakinto! Goldfish Pokémon!
Water type!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:03.700
When the weather grows warm,
they form groups and swim upriver!

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.710
This sight serves as a poetic reminder
that spring has arrived!

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:10.120
This... isn’t the Lord, is it?

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.590
Well, I fished it,
may as well catch it!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.980
Tosakinto’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.650
I caught Tosakinto!

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.520
I got something, too!

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:29.650
Come on!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.280
Koiking!

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:37.190
Koiking! Fish Pokémon!
Water type!

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:42.910
It is virtually worthless in terms of both power and speed,
the most weak and pathetic Pokémon in the world!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.980
This isn’t it either...

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.400
Can I catch it, Satoshi?

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.690
Sure, go ahead!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.930
Thanks!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.310
Koiking’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.380
I caught Koiking!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.300
And I’m gonna fish up the Lord, too!

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.620
Got a bite!

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.520
Me, too!

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.650
Again?!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.030
I’ve caught them already,
so let’s release them.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:22.090
Hey, do you think
this Lord really exists?

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.890
It has to!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.790
Maybe I’ll try another lure...

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.800
I’m counting on you, Octan lure!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.400
Ah! That’s my number one
recommended lure!

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.180
So what exactly?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.140
Here goes!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.950
W-What is this?!
It’s nothing like the others!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.280
Go! Don’t let go!

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:48.150
I know!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.770
Oh!

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.690
Good timing!
Can you help us?!

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.820
Hurry up! Hurry up,
or it’s gonna get away!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.820
Not if I can help it!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:04.700
Why exactly do we have to
do this, meow...?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.460
Going with the flow?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.390
We did it!

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.580
Whoa! It’s huge!

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:14.420
Could this be it?

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.440
That’s...

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.850
It’s the Lord!
Those kids fished it up!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.210
Huh? It’s really the Lord?

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:27.940
How is it <i>that</i> huge?!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.270
All right, I’m gonna catch it!
Go!

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:38.150
I’ll battle you then! Koiking’s a Water type!
I’ll use a Grass type then!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.950
Go, Nazonokusa!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.920
It’s gonna Flop again!

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.290
I won’t let it!
Nazonokusa! Sleep Powder!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.780
Now! Monster Ball!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.050
Nice!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:07.680
All right!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.930
You did it, Go!

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.430
I’m exhausted, meow.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.290
Thank you!

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:19.450
If you guys hadn’t been there to help,
I couldn’t have fished up that Koiking!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.700
Oh, I’m glad I could
be of help, me lads.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.490
Yeah, me lads.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.200
Well, me lads,
we should be off.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.420
What was that?!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.670
It came from the hotel!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.180
My Eevee’s in there!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.240
Group 1,
take them to the back immediately.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.970
Group 2, move out.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:52.560
<i>Yes, ma’am!</i>

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.240
Team Rocket!

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:55.560
They’re Team Rocket, too?!

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:59.090
That bowl-headed four-eyes
followed us here, didn’t she?!

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:03.320
No, it looks like some large-scale
Pokémon capture operation.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.230
Nobody told <i>us!</i>

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:07.620
So they didn’t want
our help, meow?!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.420
Capture complete.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.000
Good work.
That did go smoothly.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Having our problems go on a “break”
was the right choice.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:18.760
Begin cleanup.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:19.310
Ma’am.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.630
Hold it!

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.410
Give everyone’s Pokémon back!

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.650
Eliminate them.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.140
Ma’am.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.310
<i>Go!</i>

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.850
Riolu, I choose you!

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:35.420
Pikachu!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.980
Rabbifoot, don’t lose!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.460
PocketMonsters

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:44.270
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:48.580
PocketMonsters

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:53.500
. Normal .
Nyarth
PocketMonsters

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.500
Should we just watch?
Or should we help?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.420
She didn’t want our help in the first place,
even in this huge operation!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.010
By getting rid of “problems”,
she meant <i>us</i>, meow!

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:09.260
That bowl-headed four-eyes
is trying to take the glory for herself!

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.770
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!
Riolu! Vacuum Wave!

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.990
Dokurog! Sludge Bomb!

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.280
Pikachu!

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.040
Bunyat! Erratic Scratch!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:35.670
Riolu!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.340
Rabbifoot!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.340
I’m not gonna lose! Pikachu!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:48.850
Venom Shock!

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.310
Are you okay?!

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.800
Skutank! Flamethrower!

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:06.150
They don’t call them the elite unit for nothing!
They’re strong, meow.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.530
Don’t be impressed!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.050
Pikachu!

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.340
Hold on, Satoshi,
it’s dangerous!

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:13.290
Pikachu!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.670
Oh, they got Pikachu, too!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.710
What should we do?

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.540
I don’t know what to say, meow.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.800
What happened here?

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.300
Unacceptable!

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.540
That bowl-headed four-eyes’s
gonna take all the glory for herself!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.090
I’m not gonna just stand about
and watch, meow.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.800
Makes you want
some revenge, yeah?

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:06.830
I got it!

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:07.760
You thought of something?

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:11.380
A plan that’ll make that bowl-headed four-eyes
throw in the towel!

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.890
I’m gonna go save Pikachu!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.510
But we don’t even know
where they went!

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:20.270
Still, I’ve gotta save him!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.270
Brave, aren’t you, me lads?
I like that, me lads.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.900
We’ll help you out, me lads!

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.280
What do you mean?

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.740
Heading straight at them
is pointless, me lads.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.010
You need to use your mind.
Think!

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.780
Actually,
in the confusion earlier, me lads,

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.910
I put a tracker on
one of their Pokémon, me lads.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:41.790
So we know
where they went, me lads.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.290
Really?!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.310
While one of you acts as a decoy,

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:49.670
the other one sneaks in and
saves the Pokémon, me lads. You in?

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:50.800
I’ll do it!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.930
Me, too, of course!

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.660
Then, let’s go, me lads!

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:03.420
So, we have the brat boys
save the Pokémon...

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.940
...and then,
we’ll take the lot.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.360
I can just <i>see</i> her face, meow!

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.010
You’re useless!

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.740
I’m very sorry.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:17.620
And in comparison, look at how many Pokémon
you’ve caught for us. Incredible, Musashi!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.790
Oh, it was nothing at all!

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:23.920
Kojiro! You’re my number one
most-reliable agent!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.790
Thank you!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:29.170
Nyarth... Isn’t that nice...

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.800
Sakaki...!

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:47.030
Pikachu...

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:47.950
Now.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:48.660
Right.

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.380
Hey! Team Rocket!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.580
Who are <i>you?!</i>

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.720
Come out!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.460
You’re up, Koiking!

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.300
Pikachu!

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:15.260
Hold on, I’ll open it up now!

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.510
Leave it to me, me lad.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:22.220
Come on, me lad,
you won’t get this open with brute force.

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:27.650
Everyone, run for it!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:29.820
Quietly, me lads.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.830
Pikachu. Here, eat this.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.580
What’re you trying to pull?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.330
Here’s what!
Koiking! Flop!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.010
No way...!

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:57.810
What’s going on?

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.800
Hurry, everyone!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:01.760
Hey, you!

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.260
Oh no, they spotted me!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.150
I’ll make you give
everyone’s Pokémon back!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.210
Get him.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.110
Ma’am!

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.240
I won’t let you have your way!

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.240
Hmph! What can a child do?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.660
Bunyat! Slash!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.430
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:33.290
What are you doing?!
It’s just a single Pikachu!

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.170
Everyone!

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:45.720
T-This...

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:46.930
Do it!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.030
M-Matori.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.880
You’re under arrest
for stealing Pokémon!

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.330
Retreat!

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.520
Ma’am!
Dosaidon! Stone Edge!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.510
Stop!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.890
<i>See ya!</i>

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.200
Thank you for all your help.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.410
It’s nothing...

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.710
Thank you! We couldn’t have saved
Pikachu and the Pokémon without you!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.290
Well, we just did
what anyone would, me lads...

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.800
With Junsa here, taking the lot...

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.170
...isn’t gonna happen, meow.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.540
We should get going, then.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:00.920
Oh, at least tell me your names!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:05.020
If you ask us
“At least tell me your nam—”

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:07.510
It’s really nothing worth
remembering us for, me lads!

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:10.210
They were really nice,
weren’t they?

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.070
Yeah!

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.880
Hi, Musashi here!

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:20.920
You were unusually quick today.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:25.570
Naturally! We’re all refreshed from our break
and full of motivation!

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.680
Oh, but Lady Matori,
you’re looking tired today.

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:31.230
Have you considered taking a break?

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.920
I don’t have time to relax.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:38.050
I’ll tell Sakaki that you’re back
on your mission.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:39.670
Sure!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.070
You saw it, right? Her face...

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:44.550
She must’ve gotten
scolded real bad by Sakaki!

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:48.250
She messed up an important scheme,
so naturally, meow!

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:53.250
Serves her right!
We’re the ones Team Rocket really needs!

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:57.820
Now, we let him go
during our break,

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.820
but next time,
we’re catching that Pikachu!

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.690
Yeah!

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.130
Are you okay, Pikachu?

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:08.310
So this Koiking was “The Lord”.

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.830
It’s got quite the size.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.510
Other than the size,
it looks like an ordinary Koiking, though...

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.490
Well, that <i>is</i> amazing.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:31.060
Isn’t it just? We had these incredibly kind people
help us catch it, me lads!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.770
Incredibly... Wait, “me lads”?

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:36.110
Yeah! And they helped
when we battled Team Rocket, too...

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:39.280
Yesterday’s ally is today’s foe.

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:40.600
When they meet again,

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:43.910
Team Rocket are sure to be back
to their usual selves, me lads.

